               "secondary_keys": [],
               "content": "The Miners' Rest is the social heart of Woodmine. And for reasons. Locals gather here to share news, tell stories, enjoy a good meal, and get drunk in any of these reasons, as walking straight from The Miners' Rest leads to a bad luck and wasted money. It's a cozy, rustic tavern with a warm fireplace, wooden beams, and old mining equipment displayed as decor. The air is filled with the smell of hearty stews and freshly baked bread, and the sound of laughter and clinking mugs is ever-present. The tavern’s owner, an elderly woman named Betty, is a walking encyclopedia of town history and gossip. And she also has a very keen eye on people.",
