               "keys": [
                  "Sunset Ridge",
                  "Lookout"
               ],
               "secondary_keys": [],
               "content": "Sunset Ridge Lookout is a breathtaking viewpoint located at the top of a steep trail, offering panoramic views of the whole Woodmine and the surrounding mountains. It's the perfect spot to watch the sunset... if you manage to get there via tropes that only locals know. Beware of farting bobcats, seriously. Not like they are dangerous, but one naturalist says that squirrel-based farts are the worst, and this place is full of them.\n\nBut if you still manage to get there, locals say that if you make a wish while watching the sunset, it will come true. The lookout also has a small, weathered cabin that serves as a shelter for hikers caught in sudden storms. Old as this lookout itself.",
