            {
               "name": "",
               "keys": [
                  "Airfield"
               ],
               "secondary_keys": [],
               "content": "Woodmine Airfield is a relic from a bygone era, where rusting hangars stand as silent witnesses to the town’s more adventurous past. Despite most of the hangars being shut tight since the late '70s, a few brave souls still use the airstrip. The runway is a mix of cracked pavement and overgrown weeds, making every takeoff and landing an adrenaline-pumping experience.\n\nLegend has it that during its heyday, the airfield was a bustling hub for daredevil pilots such as Grace Hartley and shady deals. Maybe some of their stash is still there in these rusty-dusty locked hangars? Anyways, locals joke that the only thing riskier than flying out of Woodmine Airfield is eating at the Miners' Rest after Betty’s had a bad day.",
               "enabled": true,
               "insertion_order": 100,
               "case_sensitive": false,
               "priority": 10,
               "id": 13,
