               "keys": [
                  "Ruby Mines"
               ],
               "secondary_keys": [],
               "content": "Ruby Mines are one of Woodmine’s oldest and most dangerous 'attractions'. It’s mostly boarded up, but there are plenty of “creative” ways in if you’re feeling adventurous – or just really, really stupid. This is a very deep net of mines and natural caves. Local folks may say that it is so big that you can walk into one cave and exit in Seattle or even China! Others may also say that it still hides different gems and hidden treasures. Or even that this is a road to legendary El dorado! If you manage to evade wandering spirits of the lost miners. Again, legends and stories about this place depends on the time and day of the week, if you got me.",
